{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:1.1-4", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-4"}, "paraphrase": "King Bṛhadratha renounces and does austerity; Śākāyanya teaches him: through austerity comes sattva, through sattva mind, through mind the Self; like fire without fuel the mind calms in its source.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:sakayanya", "tch:brhadratha"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:1.13", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.13"}, "paraphrase": "Followers of caste and stage-duties obtain the fruit of their acts; the knower is beyond them.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:ativarnasrami"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:1.5", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.5"}, "paraphrase": "Mind (citta) alone is saṃsāra; it should be purified with effort; one becomes what one thinks.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:mind-cause-of-bondage-and-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.1", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1"}, "paraphrase": "Mahādeva teaches Maitreya: the body is called a temple, and the jīva in it is Śiva alone; one should cast off the withered flowers of ignorance and worship with the thought 'I am He'.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "original": {"text": "deho devālayaḥ proktaḥ sa jīvaḥ kevalaḥ śivaḥ | tyajed ajñānanirmālyaṃ so 'haṃbhāvena pūjayet", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:body-as-temple"], "teachers": ["tch:siva", "tch:maitreya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.13-14", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.13-14"}, "paraphrase": "'Mother delusion has died, son knowledge is born — with both impurities how shall I perform the twilight rite? The sun of consciousness shines ever in the heart-space; it neither sets nor rises — how shall I perform it?'", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.17", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.17"}, "paraphrase": "Renunciation is not the abandoning of rites nor the uttering of the renunciation formula; renunciation is the union of the individual Self and the supreme.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "original": {"text": "karmatyāgān na saṃnyāso na preṣoccāraṇena tu | sandhau jīvātmanor aikyaṃ saṃnyāsaḥ parikīrtitaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa"], "disputes": ["dsp:when-to-renounce"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.18-20", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.18-20"}, "paraphrase": "He is fit for renunciation to whom all desires seem like vomit and who has given up identifying with the body; one who renounces for food or fame falls from both worlds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:who-may-renounce"], "obstacles": ["obs:ascetic-hypocrisy"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.2", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.2"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge is seeing non-difference; meditation is a mind without objects; bathing is abandoning the mind's impurity; purity is restraint of the senses.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.21", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.21"}, "paraphrase": "The highest is reflection on truth, the middle study of scripture, the lowest mantra-recitation, and the lowest of the low wandering to tīrthas.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-tirthas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.22", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.22"}, "paraphrase": "Those who do not see the Self within are like one who sees a fruit's reflection in water and reaches for it.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.26", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.26"}, "paraphrase": "For one seeking liberation, worship in images of stone, metal or clay leads to rebirth; the renouncer should worship only in the heart.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:images-for-the-ignorant"], "disputes": ["dsp:image-worship-and-inner-worship"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.27", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.27"}, "paraphrase": "Like a pot in space, empty within and without, full within and without.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:2.3-9", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.3-9"}, "paraphrase": "He should drink the nectar of Brahman as alms and live alone; the body is impure from its origin — true purity is of the Self.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:body-foulness-contemplation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:maitreya-upanisad:3", "source": "src:maitreya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "Litany of self-knowledge: 'I am I, and also another… I am Brahman'.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
